  "notes": "Maize grain yield from Table 2 (90% N rate = standard). Biochar applied once in April 2007 (except 1 t/ha annual). p(biochar effect) = 0.54 (2007), 0.33 (2008), 0.66 (2009), 0.49 (2010) - none significant. Table 3 has data at varying N rates for 0 and 12 t/ha biochar - also no significant biochar effects. Fertile temperate soil (pH 7.36, CEC 97.6). Conclusion: biochar up to 30 t/ha does not affect yield in fertile temperate soils. Low 2007 yields due to hot dry weather after fertilization."
